==Icelandic==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|non|is}} {{term|hófr|lang=non}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|is}} {{recons|hōfaz|lang=gem-pro}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|is}} {{recons|kōpos|lang=ine-pro}}. Whence also Old English {{term|hof|hōf|lang=ang}} (English {{term|hoof|lang=en}}); Old High German {{term|huof}} (German {{term|Huf|lang=de}}); Old Saxon {{term|hof}} (Dutch {{term|hoef}}).

